{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_http_middleware_rate_limit_ratelimit", "label": "rateLimit", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Handler-Wrapper statt globaler Middleware, damit unterschiedliche Handler unterschiedliche Budgets bekommen; der Zaehler liegt in der Cache-Abstraktion, sodass Single-Pod den Speicher und Multi-Pod Redis nutzt.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/http/middleware/rate-limit.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_http_middleware_rate_limit_ratelimitoptions", "label": "RateLimitOptions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/http/middleware/rate-limit.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_http_middleware_rate_limit_ratelimitcontext", "label": "RateLimitContext", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/http/middleware/rate-limit.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_http_middleware_rate_limit_fixed_window_counting", "label": "Fixed-Window-Zaehlung", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Atomares incr mit TTL im Cache. Randeffekte an Fenstergrenzen (bis zu 2x max in zwei Sekunden) werden bewusst in Kauf genommen \u2014 eine Sliding-Window- oder Token-Bucket-Variante liefert das Framework nicht.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/http/middleware/rate-limit.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_http_middleware_rate_limit_unspoofable_key", "label": "Nicht faelschbarer Rate-Limit-Key", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "x-forwarded-for ist client-setzbar, wenn kein vertrauenswuerdiger Proxy ihn ueberschreibt; ein Angreifer rotiert ihn pro Request und umgeht das Limit. Deshalb der Socket-Peer request.remoteAddress als Default-Key.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/http/middleware/rate-limit.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_http_middleware_rate_limit_cluster_wide_rate_limiting", "label": "Cluster-faehiges Rate-Limiting", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Mit Redis-Backing teilen sich alle Pods einen Zaehler; mit InMemoryCache hat jeder Pod seinen eigenen, ein ueber 4 Pods verteilter Client bekommt also effektiv das 4-fache Limit.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/http/middleware/rate-limit.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_http_middleware_rate_limit_shared_cache_eviction_hazard", "label": "Eigene Cache-Instanz fuer den Limiter", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "InMemoryCache evictet LRU, ohne zu wissen, welcher Eintrag Sicherheits-State traegt. Ein Aufrufer, der ueber cached oder idempotent eindeutige Keys erzeugt, evictet die Zaehler anderer Clients und schenkt ihnen ein frisches Budget; der eigene Zaehler des Fluters ueberlebt, weil incr ihn bei jedem Request als zuletzt genutzt markiert.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/http/middleware/rate-limit.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_http_middleware_rate_limit_rate_limit_response_headers", "label": "X-RateLimit-Header und Retry-After", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/http/middleware/rate-limit.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_http_middleware_rate_limit_ratelimit", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_http_middleware_rate_limit_ratelimitoptions", "re